  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding Movements to Advance Rights &amp; Inclusion of All Persons with Disabilities (Global) 2020-24</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central to Australia&#x2019;s approach to disability inclusion is supporting organisations of people with disability (OPDs) in developing countries to build their capacity so they can give voice to people with disabilities at all levels and contribute as leaders and decision makers in their communities. Disability Rights Advocacy Fund (DRAF) is one of DFAT&#x2019;s global strategic partners in disability-inclusive development. Through grants, advocacy and technical assistance, DRAF provides a comprehensive approach to supporting the rights of people with disabilities through support to OPDs. Australia has supported DRAF since 2009 and continuing the partnership is consistent with DFAT&#x2019;s International Disability Equity and Rights Strategy 2025. DRAF&#x2019;s priorities, such as improving inclusion of a diverse range of people with disabilities and addressing the intersectionality of gender and disability, align closely with the guiding principles of DFAT&#x2019;s Development for All Strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
